window.products.push({"id":130217,"name":"240323002 Frigidaire Refrigerator Door Bin Bottom Shelf Replacement Part FGHS2631PF3 FGHS2631PF4A FGHS2655PF5A FGUS2642LF2 FRS6LF7JM3 LGUS2642LF2 FGHS","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":17.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51JiizHiavS._AC_SL1280_.jpg","description":"💡 Frigidaire Refrigerator Door Bin 240323002 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP2115742, 240323005, 240323006, 240323009, 240323010, 890955, AH429725, EA429725, PS429725. Door Bin 240323002 is compatible with Frigidaire, Crosley, Kenmore appliances. Frigidaire Part 240323002 is located on the bottom of the refrigerator door and is designed to hold larger items such as gallon jugs, milk cartons, and other bulky containers. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the 240323002 Door Bin? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Frigidaire 240323002 will help if your previous part is broken, leaking, or missing. Installation of the Frigidaire 240323002 Door Bin is a simple process that does not require any tools. Make sure to install the shelf securely and level before placing any items on it. 💡 Frigidaire 240323002 Door Bin For Refrigerator is made of high-quality, durable materials that are built to withstand the weight of heavy items. The shelf is made of clear plastic, which allows for easy visibility of the items stored inside. Ensure that the replacement shelf is compatible with your Frigidaire refrigerator model. 240323002 Frigidaire Refrigerator Door Bin Replacement meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Proper maintenance of the Frigidaire Door Bin 240323002 is essential to ensure its longevity and functionality. To clean the 240323002 Frigidaire Door Bin, remove it from the door and wash it with warm, soapy water. Avoid using abrasive or harsh cleaning products that may damage the shelf. Allow the shelf to air dry before replacing it on the door. Regular cleaning and inspection of the bin and the door shelf supports can help prevent damage and prolong the life of the door bin. 💡 How do you install Frigidaire refrigerator shelves? To install the 240323002 Refrigerator Door Bin first remove the old or broken shelf from the refrigerator. Depending on the model, you may need to gently lift the shelf up and out of the brackets or slide it to one side to release it. Place the new shelf onto the brackets on the refrigerator wall or door. Make sure it is level and properly aligned with the other shelves. Slide the shelf back into the brackets until it clicks into place.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51JiizHiavS._AC_SL1280_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07NNBPSMQ","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-130217","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07NNBPSMQ","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07NNBPSMQ","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
